{"id":"postahc","title":"postahc.x","program":"postahc.x","package":"PHonon","version":"7.5","html":"<section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-intro\" id=\"intro\" data-kind=\"intro\" data-title=\"Introduction\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\">Introduction</h2>\n\n<div class=\"qe-indent\"><p class=\"qe-flow\"><b>Purpose of postahc.x:</b></p>\n<pre class=\"qe-pre\">- Read the electron-phonon quantities calculated by <b>ph.x</b> with the\n<b>electron_phonon='ahc'</b> option.\n\n- Calculate the phonon-induced electron self-energy in the full matrix form\nat a given temperature.\n\n<b>Structure of the input data:</b>\n========================================================================\n\n<b>&amp;INPUT</b>\n   ...specs of namelist variables...\n<b>/</b></pre></div>\n</section>\n   <section class=\"qe-section qe-sec-namelist\" id=\"INPUT\" data-kind=\"namelist\" data-title=\"&amp;INPUT\" data-name=\"INPUT\"><h2 class=\"qe-section-title\"><span class=\"qe-kind\">Namelist</span> <span class=\"qe-nl\">&amp;INPUT</span></h2><div class=\"qe-layout\">\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"prefix\" data-var=\"prefix\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#prefix\">prefix</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"prefix\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>'pwscf'</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Prepended to input/output filenames; must be the same\nused in the calculation of unperturbed system.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"outdir\" data-var=\"outdir\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#outdir\">outdir</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"outdir\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd><span class=\"qe-flow\">value of the <code>ESPRESSO_TMPDIR</code> environment variable if set;\n<br> current directory ('./') otherwise</span></dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Directory containing input, output, and scratch files;\nmust be the same as specified in the calculation of\nthe unperturbed system.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"ahc_dir\" data-var=\"ahc_dir\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#ahc_dir\">ahc_dir</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">REQUIRED</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"ahc_dir\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Directory where the binary files are located.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"use_irr_q\" data-var=\"use_irr_q\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#use_irr_q\">use_irr_q</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"use_irr_q\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.false.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">If .true., assume that the q points are on the irreducible grid. In this case,\nthe data in <a href=\"#ahc_dir\" data-local=\"ahc_dir\">ahc_dir</a> must have been actually generated from a calculation\non an irreducible q grid.\nOff-diagonal self-energies cannot be computed if use_irr_q = .true.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"ahc_nbnd\" data-var=\"ahc_nbnd\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#ahc_nbnd\">ahc_nbnd</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">REQUIRED</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"ahc_nbnd\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Number of bands for which the electron self-energy is to be computed. Must be\nidentical to ahc_nbnd of the ph.x run with electron_phonon='ahc'.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"ahc_nbndskip\" data-var=\"ahc_nbndskip\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#ahc_nbndskip\">ahc_nbndskip</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">INTEGER</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"ahc_nbndskip\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>0</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Number of bands to exclude when computing the self-energy. Must be identical to\nahc_nbndskip of the ph.x run with electron_phonon='ahc'.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"flvec\" data-var=\"flvec\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#flvec\">flvec</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">CHARACTER</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">REQUIRED</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"flvec\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">File containing the normalized phonon displacements written by matdyn.x.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"eta_eV\" data-var=\"eta_eV\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#eta_eV\">eta_eV</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">REQUIRED</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"eta_eV\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Magnitude of the small imaginary component included to smooth the energy\ndenominators, in eV.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"temp_kelvin\" data-var=\"temp_kelvin\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#temp_kelvin\">temp_kelvin</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">REQUIRED</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"temp_kelvin\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Temperature in Kelvins at which the electron self-energy is calculated.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"efermi_eV\" data-var=\"efermi_eV\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#efermi_eV\">efermi_eV</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">REQUIRED</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"efermi_eV\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Fermi energy of the electrons in eV.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"amass_amu\" data-var=\"amass_amu\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#amass_amu\">amass_amu(i), i=1,ntyp</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-status\">REQUIRED</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"amass_amu\"></span></header><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Mass for each atom type in atomic mass unit.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"ahc_win_min_eV\" data-var=\"ahc_win_min_eV\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#ahc_win_min_eV\">ahc_win_min_eV</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"ahc_win_min_eV\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>-1.d8</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Lower bound of active AHC window for the lower Fan term in eV.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"ahc_win_max_eV\" data-var=\"ahc_win_max_eV\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#ahc_win_max_eV\">ahc_win_max_eV</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">REAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"ahc_win_max_eV\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>1.d8</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">Upper bound of active AHC window for the lower Fan term in eV.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"skip_upper\" data-var=\"skip_upper\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#skip_upper\">skip_upper</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"skip_upper\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.false.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">If .true., skip calculation of the upper Fan self-energy. Also, truncate the<br>Debye-Waller self-energy to include only the low-energy band contribution.\n(Corresponds to the second term (lower Fan + lower DW) of Eq. (G1-revised) of<br>J.-M. Lihm and C.-H. Park, PRX 12, 039901(E) (2022).)\nIf .false., calculate the contribution of both the high-energy and low-energy\nbands. In this case, ahc_upfan_iq#.bin files must be present in <a href=\"#ahc_dir\" data-local=\"ahc_dir\">ahc_dir</a>.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"skip_dw\" data-var=\"skip_dw\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#skip_dw\">skip_dw</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"skip_dw\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.false.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">If .true., skip calculation of the Debye-Waller self-energy.\nIf .false., ahc_dw.bin file must be present in <a href=\"#ahc_dir\" data-local=\"ahc_dir\">ahc_dir</a>.</p></div></article>\n\n      <article class=\"qe-var\" id=\"adiabatic\" data-var=\"adiabatic\"><header class=\"qe-var-head\"><h3 class=\"qe-var-name\"><a class=\"qe-self\" href=\"#adiabatic\">adiabatic</a></h3> <span class=\"qe-type\" title=\"Fortran type\">LOGICAL</span> <span class=\"qe-var-tools\" data-var=\"adiabatic\"></span></header><dl class=\"qe-meta\"><div class=\"qe-meta-row qe-meta-default\"><dt>Default</dt><dd>.false.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"qe-desc\"><p class=\"qe-flow\">If .true., use the adiabatic approximation when computing the Fan self-energy\nby ignoring the phonon frequency in the denominator. This approximation is known\nto be inaccurate and even divergent in some materials (S. PoncÃ© et al., J. Chem.\nPhys. 143, 102813 (2015)). Therefore, this keyword should be used only for\nexperimental or debugging purposes.</p></div></article>\n\n   </div></section>","sections":[{"id":"intro","title":"Introduction","kind":"intro","level":0,"varIds":[]},{"id":"INPUT","title":"&INPUT","kind":"namelist","name":"INPUT","level":0,"varIds":["prefix","outdir","ahc_dir","use_irr_q","ahc_nbnd","ahc_nbndskip","flvec","eta_eV","temp_kelvin","efermi_eV","amass_amu","ahc_win_min_eV","ahc_win_max_eV","skip_upper","skip_dw","adiabatic"]}],"variables":[{"id":"prefix","names":["prefix"],"display":"prefix","type":"CHARACTER","default":"'pwscf'","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Prepended to input/output filenames; must be the same used in the calculation of unperturbed system."},{"id":"outdir","names":["outdir"],"display":"outdir","type":"CHARACTER","default":"value of the ESPRESSO_TMPDIR environment variable if set; current directory ('./') otherwise","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Directory containing input, output, and scratch files; must be the same as specified in the calculation of the unperturbed system."},{"id":"ahc_dir","names":["ahc_dir"],"display":"ahc_dir","type":"CHARACTER","status":"REQUIRED","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Directory where the binary files are located."},{"id":"use_irr_q","names":["use_irr_q"],"display":"use_irr_q","type":"LOGICAL","default":".false.","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"If .true., assume that the q points are on the irreducible grid."},{"id":"ahc_nbnd","names":["ahc_nbnd"],"display":"ahc_nbnd","type":"INTEGER","status":"REQUIRED","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Number of bands for which the electron self-energy is to be computed."},{"id":"ahc_nbndskip","names":["ahc_nbndskip"],"display":"ahc_nbndskip","type":"INTEGER","default":"0","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Number of bands to exclude when computing the self-energy."},{"id":"flvec","names":["flvec"],"display":"flvec","type":"CHARACTER","status":"REQUIRED","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"File containing the normalized phonon displacements written by matdyn.x."},{"id":"eta_eV","names":["eta_eV"],"display":"eta_eV","type":"REAL","status":"REQUIRED","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Magnitude of the small imaginary component included to smooth the energy denominators, in eV."},{"id":"temp_kelvin","names":["temp_kelvin"],"display":"temp_kelvin","type":"REAL","status":"REQUIRED","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Temperature in Kelvins at which the electron self-energy is calculated."},{"id":"efermi_eV","names":["efermi_eV"],"display":"efermi_eV","type":"REAL","status":"REQUIRED","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Fermi energy of the electrons in eV."},{"id":"amass_amu","names":["amass_amu"],"display":"amass_amu(i), i=1,ntyp","type":"REAL","status":"REQUIRED","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Mass for each atom type in atomic mass unit."},{"id":"ahc_win_min_eV","names":["ahc_win_min_eV"],"display":"ahc_win_min_eV","type":"REAL","default":"-1.d8","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Lower bound of active AHC window for the lower Fan term in eV."},{"id":"ahc_win_max_eV","names":["ahc_win_max_eV"],"display":"ahc_win_max_eV","type":"REAL","default":"1.d8","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"Upper bound of active AHC window for the lower Fan term in eV."},{"id":"skip_upper","names":["skip_upper"],"display":"skip_upper","type":"LOGICAL","default":".false.","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"If .true., skip calculation of the upper Fan self-energy."},{"id":"skip_dw","names":["skip_dw"],"display":"skip_dw","type":"LOGICAL","default":".false.","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"If .true., skip calculation of the Debye-Waller self-energy."},{"id":"adiabatic","names":["adiabatic"],"display":"adiabatic","type":"LOGICAL","default":".false.","sectionId":"INPUT","sectionTitle":"&INPUT","options":[],"summary":"If .true., use the adiabatic approximation when computing the Fan self-energy by ignoring the phonon frequency in the denominator."}],"aliases":{"id3":"prefix","prefix":"prefix","id4":"outdir","outdir":"outdir","id5":"ahc_dir","ahc_dir":"ahc_dir","id6":"use_irr_q","use_irr_q":"use_irr_q","id7":"ahc_nbnd","ahc_nbnd":"ahc_nbnd","id8":"ahc_nbndskip","ahc_nbndskip":"ahc_nbndskip","id9":"flvec","flvec":"flvec","id10":"eta_eV","eta_eV":"eta_eV","id11":"temp_kelvin","temp_kelvin":"temp_kelvin","id12":"efermi_eV","efermi_eV":"efermi_eV","id13":"amass_amu","amass_amu":"amass_amu","id14":"ahc_win_min_eV","ahc_win_min_eV":"ahc_win_min_eV","id15":"ahc_win_max_eV","ahc_win_max_eV":"ahc_win_max_eV","id16":"skip_upper","skip_upper":"skip_upper","id17":"skip_dw","skip_dw":"skip_dw","id18":"adiabatic","adiabatic":"adiabatic","id2":"INPUT","INPUT":"INPUT","id1":"intro"}}